{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And HaShem showed him all, etc.</b> The meaning is that HaShem activated within him a power of sight such as the eye has no boundary to see, in one of two ways: either He illuminated his eyes with the sown light reserved for the righteous, which is the light of the six days of Genesis stored away for the righteous, concerning which our Sages of blessed memory said (Ḥagigah 12a) that through it a person can gaze from one end of the world to the other; or He drew the earth near before his eyes and showed it to him right in front of him:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:28.385906824Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}